# Trivy ignore list (docker.yml scans api/web images).
#
# Rule: only add an entry here for a specific, reviewed, accepted finding,
# with the advisory ID and a reason. NEVER add broad patterns or the whole
# file — the point of the gate is to fail on new fixable HIGH/CRITICALs.
#
# Format (see trivy docs):
#   CVE-2025-XXXXX   # reason, tracked in docs/security.md
#
# Currently empty — all fixable HIGH/CRITICAL findings must be fixed by
# bumping a base-image digest (see Dockerfiles "bump:" comments) or a
# dependency pin. Unfixable findings are already filtered by
# ignore-unfixed: true in the workflow.
